<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Laguatan</h1><p class="st-meta">400 CE – 700 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A great Berber confederation of the Libyan desert that fought Byzantine Africa and survived as the Lawata tribe of Arab writers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Laguatan (Leuathae in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a>, Lawata in Arabic sources) were a confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camel</a>-using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribes that moved west from the Syrtic region and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> in the 5th and 6th centuries, perhaps including the earlier <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/austuriani">Austuriani</a>. They first appear as a serious power in the wars of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/praetorian-prefecture-of-africa">Byzantine Africa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation was led by chiefs, and its leader Ierna was also priest of the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurzil">Gurzil</a>, whose image was carried into battle, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corippus">Corippus</a>. In 543 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> killed Laguatan envoys at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/leptis-magna">Leptis Magna</a>, setting off a long war. The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-troglita">John Troglita</a> defeated them and their allies in 546 to 548, after which they paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Laguatan remained powerful in the desert. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> arrived in the 640s, the Lawata were among the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> they met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania">Tripolitania</a>; many converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, later often to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibadism">Ibadism</a>, and Lawata groups spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 CE – 700 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:67.66%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 CE – 700 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ierna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Berber religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a>, <a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Leuathae, Lawata, Ilaguas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=550&amp;focus=laguatan" aria-label="Laguatan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5155 1192 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Laguatan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5475 1448h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5475 1448h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Libya. <a href="/atlas?year=550&amp;focus=laguatan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

